      "content": "The thing is, the actual numbers aren't exactly \"massive\"—the coral health increase was only about 5% after the last cycle. That's way below the 20% we were aiming for. If we just list \"5%,\" I'm worried the GEF will think we're ineffective and deny us the money. \n\nHow can we write this section so they still see us as a \"high-impact\" org? Is there a way to frame that 5% growth so it sounds like a huge win instead of a disappointment? I need this grant to go through.",
